usb-storage: Disable UAS for the VIA VL817 SATA bridge

Backport upstream commits 5b67b315037250a61861119683e7fcb509deea25
and 609865ab3d5d803556f628e221ecd3d06aed9f30 together. The bridge can
stall and reset during writes with UAS. Match USB ID 2109:0715 for
the full upstream firmware revision range.

Put the quirk in unusual_uas.h so the 4.9 UAS driver sees it during
both the boot eligibility check and normal probing. usb-storage
can then bind the bridge using its standard Bulk-Only match.

diff --git a/drivers/usb/storage/unusual_uas.h b/drivers/usb/storage/unusual_uas.h
--- a/drivers/usb/storage/unusual_uas.h
+++ b/drivers/usb/storage/unusual_uas.h
@@ -184,6 +184,13 @@
 		USB_SC_DEVICE, USB_PR_DEVICE, NULL,
 		US_FL_NO_ATA_1X),
 
+/* The VL817 can stall and reset under UAS. */
+UNUSUAL_DEV(0x2109, 0x0715, 0x0000, 0x9999,
+		"VIA Labs, Inc.",
+		"VL817 SATA Bridge",
+		USB_SC_DEVICE, USB_PR_DEVICE, NULL,
+		US_FL_IGNORE_UAS),
+
 /* Reported-by: Icenowy Zheng <icenowy@aosc.io> */
 UNUSUAL_DEV(0x2537, 0x1068, 0x0000, 0x9999,
 		"Norelsys",
